                <pb facs="0530" n="502" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v04/pg502"/>

                <head>210. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On January 15, the Department of State issued a press release stating United
                    States views on and support for the proposed European Common Market and Free
                    Trade Area. For text of the statement, see Department of State <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, February 4, 1957, page 182. In telegram
                    1910 to Bonn, January 11, also sent to the Embassies in the other five ECSC
                    countries as well as the United Kingdom, the Department transmitted an advance
                    text of the statement, and authorized the addressees to inform the respective
                    Foreign Offices informally <pb facs="0531" n="503" xml:id="pg503"/> of the
                    timing of the announcement and to make the text available. (Department of State,
                    Central Files, 840.05/1–1157)</p>
            </div>
